{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries meaningful signal for this task at all. This is the most consequential design decision: it determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing and which branch of the configuration space to prioritize. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001—same profile setting, same structural simplicity (no aggregation/fusion needed)—isolating the effect of modality. If image-only substantially outperforms RNA-only, multimodal fusion configs become high-priority; if it underperforms, we should invest in RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) instead. ResNet50 is a standard, well-calibrated image encoder appropriate for a first modality probe. Under a tight budget, resolving which modality is stronger before committing to complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations is the highest-information-value next step."
}

